WEBVTT

00:04.650 --> 00:07.362
This is Allen Company task training for drillers

00:07.362 --> 00:09.938
and blaster's helpers. You'll be working on top

00:09.938 --> 00:13.425
of the bench, near the edge, around explosives.

00:13.425 --> 00:15.325
Each of those is a way to get killed,

00:15.325 --> 00:16.850
so the rules here are firm.

00:17.977 --> 00:20.064
The ground near the crest can be cracked from the

00:20.064 --> 00:23.014
last shot. At Clover Bottom's surface pit,

00:23.014 --> 00:26.952
benches are about 65 feet high. Before work starts,

00:26.952 --> 00:29.964
the bench and highwall are examined for loose ground.

00:29.964 --> 00:32.952
Keep the drill at least 6 feet back from the crest,

00:32.952 --> 00:35.839
track with the mast down, and anyone working within

00:35.839 --> 00:38.027
reach of the edge where there's a danger of falling

00:38.027 --> 00:39.214
is tied off.

00:42.526 --> 00:45.226
Examine the drill before use: tracks,

00:45.226 --> 00:47.914
mast and pins, hoses and couplings,

00:47.914 --> 00:51.539
rod handling, emergency stops and the dust collector.

00:51.539 --> 00:54.514
Keep the collector skirt down and the system working.

00:54.514 --> 00:57.851
Our rock is low in silica, but drill dust is still

00:57.851 --> 01:00.414
the heaviest dust on the property. Run with the

01:00.414 --> 01:03.614
cab closed and use your respirator where required.

01:04.744 --> 01:08.332
Rotating steel grabs gloves, sleeves and rags.

01:08.332 --> 01:11.544
Stay clear while it turns. Make rod and bit changes

01:11.544 --> 01:14.244
with rotation stopped, using the tools made for

01:14.244 --> 01:14.794
it.

01:15.922 --> 01:19.434
Never drill into, or close to, a bootleg or a hole

01:19.434 --> 01:21.872
that might still hold explosives from a previous

01:21.872 --> 01:24.722
shot. If you see one, stop and report it to the

01:24.722 --> 01:25.635
blaster.

01:26.764 --> 01:29.451
Our crew also drills and blasts underground at

01:29.451 --> 01:32.814
all three sites. On the surface at Clover Bottom,

01:32.814 --> 01:35.814
a blasting contractor sometimes does the shot;

01:35.814 --> 01:38.489
follow their blaster's directions the same way.

01:38.489 --> 01:41.627
There, you drill at the face instead of on a bench.

01:41.627 --> 01:44.052
The face, back and ribs are examined,

01:44.052 --> 01:47.901
and loose rock is scaled down, before anyone drills.

01:47.901 --> 01:51.352
The same rules apply: never drill into an old hole,

01:51.352 --> 01:53.839
control the dust, and do only what the blaster

01:53.839 --> 01:54.864
assigns.

01:58.203 --> 02:00.790
On a shot, the blaster is in charge.

02:00.790 --> 02:03.390
Helpers do only what the blaster assigns.

02:03.390 --> 02:06.190
Once explosives are brought to the loading area,

02:06.190 --> 02:08.965
only work that's needed for loading is done there,

02:08.965 --> 02:11.303
and only the equipment and vehicles that are needed

02:11.303 --> 02:12.153
come in.

02:13.280 --> 02:16.555
No smoking or open flame near explosives.

02:16.555 --> 02:19.942
The loaded area is attended or barricaded and posted.

02:19.942 --> 02:22.880
Radios and phones are kept back from loaded holes,

02:22.880 --> 02:25.718
at the distance the blaster sets. If an electrical

02:25.718 --> 02:28.442
storm approaches, the area is cleared,

02:28.442 --> 02:31.593
following the blaster's direction. Handle explosives

02:31.593 --> 02:34.930
and initiators exactly as the blaster shows you;

02:34.930 --> 02:36.230
don't improvise.

02:37.359 --> 02:40.359
Before a shot, everyone is cleared out and every

02:40.359 --> 02:43.221
access road into the blast area is guarded.

02:43.221 --> 02:46.659
At Allen, the warning is the siren and strobe beacons,

02:46.659 --> 02:49.046
and underground, every entrance to the headers

02:49.046 --> 02:51.559
is blocked. If you're assigned as a guard,

02:51.559 --> 02:54.209
you stay at your post and stop everyone,

02:54.209 --> 02:57.584
no exceptions, until the blaster gives the all-clear.

02:58.700 --> 03:01.387
After the shot, no one returns until the blaster

03:01.387 --> 03:04.200
has checked the area and the fumes have cleared.

03:04.200 --> 03:07.112
Blast fumes can include carbon monoxide and nitrogen

03:07.112 --> 03:10.200
dioxide; the orange cloud is a warning.

03:10.200 --> 03:12.862
If there's a misfire, the area stays closed until

03:12.862 --> 03:14.475
the blaster deals with it.

03:17.790 --> 03:20.440
Recap: examine the bench and the drill.

03:20.440 --> 03:23.652
Stay back from the crest and tie off when required.

03:23.652 --> 03:27.277
Control drill dust. Stay clear of rotating steel.

03:27.277 --> 03:30.102
Never drill into an old hole. On a shot,

03:30.102 --> 03:32.777
the blaster is in charge; follow the loading-area

03:32.777 --> 03:35.527
rules, guard your post, and stay out until the

03:35.527 --> 03:36.477
all-clear.

03:37.608 --> 03:40.770
Remember: your site's plans and procedures always

03:40.770 --> 03:42.270
override this video.
